                        "sense_id": "bc4d0fd7-f478-3b1f-8076-b09c2cf2825d",
                        "entry_id": "db6336a1-d21a-3b76-9d08-129bca8ed3f4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A counterbalanced structure having one end that rises as the other lowers."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ccc009b7-aa47-47c2-90c9-94d87c20e002",
                                "sense_id": "bc4d0fd7-f478-3b1f-8076-b09c2cf2825d",
                                "text": "In the late eighties and early nineties several new types of movable spans were advocated, including the pull-back draw, the jackknife span, the bob-tail swing, the horizontal-folding draw, the shearpole draw, the gyratory lift, the transbordeur, the double-cantilever swing, several types of bascule, and the vertical lift."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c2d237cc-372e-4b15-b2f7-9673cdffa0e0",
                                "sense_id": "bc4d0fd7-f478-3b1f-8076-b09c2cf2825d",
                                "text": "The study sample contains nine rolling-lift bascules of the type invented by Chicago engineer William Scherzer in 1893 , and refined by the engineering staff of the Scherzer Rolling Lift Bridge Company, also of Chicago."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dc5ec40d-97a6-4d51-a754-2281631775c3",
                                "sense_id": "bc4d0fd7-f478-3b1f-8076-b09c2cf2825d",
                                "text": "Look at those towering structures. It’s the first combination of bascule and suspension bridge ever attempted. Most innovative. [In reference to w:Tower Bridge.]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2d820735-15b8-31e8-8597-4860b078530c",
                        "entry_id": "db6336a1-d21a-3b76-9d08-129bca8ed3f4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The portion of a breech-loading firearm that pivots open in order to allow access to the chamber."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1e6568b4-78e6-48ca-bc70-bb5abd1c6fea",
                                "sense_id": "2d820735-15b8-31e8-8597-4860b078530c",
                                "text": "A device for coupling and releasing the trigger mechanism in a bascule of a gun"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
